Post-processing sources and modifications (2026 shadPS4 Emulator Project)

GSR1: https://github.com/SnapdragonGameStudios/snapdragon-gsr
Revision d926f074bcb9d714e179f1ce0fcb9ee2eeb5074e, sgsr/v1/include/hlsl.
Copyright 2023 Qualcomm Innovation Center, Inc. BSD-3-Clause; see GSR1-LICENSE.
The mobile spatial filter is wrapped as a compute shader with Vulkan bindings.

CMAA2: https://github.com/GameTechDev/CMAA2
Revision 071c6b0857559f4e36f614362e6d2aab1b61938a, Projects/CMAA2/CMAA2/CMAA2.hlsl.
Copyright 2018 Intel Corporation; author Filip Strugar.
Apache-2.0; see CMAA2-LICENSE and the retained Microsoft helper notice in cmaa2.hlsl.
A dynamic Load offset is added to the coordinates for DXC. GLSL storage formats,
bindings and zero-returning out-of-bounds loads are adapted for Vulkan. Candidate
processing and deferred color application retain the original indirect dispatches.

TDAA: https://github.com/aston89/TDAA-Temporal-Detail-Anti-Aliasing-for-ReShade
Revision d6a64774882da83bc9839bbefc5768de5b640126.
Copyright Aston89 (Baudelaire). GPL-3.0; see TDAA-LICENSE.
Temporal resolve and detail/polish are wrapped as compute shaders using the
upstream defaults. History color and state use GPU ping-pong images, replacing
the original copy pass. The first frame initializes history from the current
image. A combined binary containing TDAA and CMAA2 must use GPLv3, as permitted
by the emulator's GPL-2.0-or-later licence, retaining third-party notices.

PSMAA: https://github.com/RdenBlaauwen/PSMAA
Revision 39eb74da55c0663cef22a0f1d4a746ebf33f9e10; bundled dependencies from
the v1.0.0-beta release. Copyright 2025 Robert den Blaauwen. Original code is
MIT; see psmaa/LICENSE and psmaa/reshade-shared/LICENSE. Third-party SMAA,
FidelityFX CAS and BeanSmoothing/TSMAA notices remain in their source headers.
Seven compute passes replace ReShade passes, preserving discarded pixels and
sRGB operations. Depth modulation is disabled. Optional CAS sharpening is not
enabled; the separate host sharpening selector controls RCAS.
The BeanSmoothing/TSMAA permission remains unresolved. LicenseRef-PSMAA-ThirdParty
identifies this uncertainty; it does not grant a new redistribution permission.
This experimental integration is for the requested personal build until the
third-party permission is clarified before publication.

SMAA lookup textures: https://github.com/iryoku/smaa
Revision 71c806a838bdd7d517df19192a20f0c61b3ca29d, Textures/AreaTex.h and SearchTex.h.
MIT; copyright and full permission notices are retained in areatex.h/searchtex.h.

The generated *.comp shaders come from the retained HLSL sources. Regenerate
and validate them with Python 3 and the Vulkan SDK:
python src/video_core/host_shaders/postfx/convert.py --tools <VulkanSDK/Bin>
Normal emulator builds embed the GLSL sources and need no DXC or Python runtime.
